+### Compound Format
+
+Pass `compound: true` to get multiple parts, largest unit first. The output is compatible with Go's `time.ParseDuration`: parts have no separators and hours are the largest unit (days are not used). Zero parts are skipped, leftover milliseconds are dropped, and `compound` takes precedence over `long`.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h30m"
+ms(91800000, { compound: true })      // "25h30m"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h30m"
+ms(500, { compound: true })           // "0s"
+```
+
